# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# APPOINTMENTS - ADMIN CREATE AUTHORIZATION CHECKS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tests that non-admin mechanics cannot use POST /api/customers/{id}/appointments.
# Unauthenticated 401 coverage for this endpoint is maintained in appointments-unauth.http.
# The AdminOnly policy on this route rejects the request before the handler ever reads CustomerId/
# VehicleId from the URL, so a non-existent pair would 403 identically — CustomerId/VehicleId are
# still resolved from a real customer/vehicle at run time to keep the fixture honest and reusable if
# this file ever grows a positive case. The X-CSRF-Token header below is required even though the
# request is expected to fail: without it, CsrfDoubleSubmitMiddleware would answer 403 before the
# AdminOnly policy ever runs, which happens to share the same status code but proves the wrong thing.

@AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress = {{$processEnv AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}
@WebUI_Origin = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_WEBUI_ORIGIN}}
@NonAdminEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_MECHANIC_EMAIL}}
@NonAdminPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_MECHANIC_PASSWORD}}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [Setup][Appointments] Clear any session cookie left by a previous file (204 or 401, not asserted)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

###

### [Setup][Appointments] Login as non-admin mechanic (200 expected)
# @name nonAdminLogin
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{NonAdminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{NonAdminPassword}}"
}

{{
  exports.CsrfToken = response.headers['set-cookie']?.find(c => c.startsWith('autoservice_csrf='))?.match(/^autoservice_csrf=([^;]+)/)?.[1];
}}

?? status == 200

###

# CSRF double-submit token for the unsafe request below (see tests/CLAUDE.md Core Rules).

### [Setup][Appointments] Resolve a customer that owns a vehicle (200 expected, GET /api/customers is plain-authenticated)
# @name seedCustomers
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup][Appointments] Resolve one of that customer's vehicles (200 expected)
@CustomerId = {{seedCustomers.find(c => c.vehicleCount > 0).id}}
# @name seedVehicles
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/{{CustomerId}}/vehicles

?? status == 200

###

### [Negative][Appointments] Non-admin mechanic cannot create appointment for customer (403 expected)
# POST /api/customers/{customerId}/appointments requires AdminOnly policy.
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/customers/{{CustomerId}}/appointments
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "vehicleId": {{seedVehicles[0].id}},
  "scheduledDate": "2026-04-30T10:00:00",
  "dueDateTime": "2026-05-01T10:00:00",
  "taskDescription": "Non-admin create attempt — should be rejected with 403",
  "mechanicIds": [1]
}

?? status == 403
